  "answer": "Two small modules with two distinct bugs: `enabled()` coerces any truthy value (`'false'`, `1`) to enabled, and `display()` returns `'ON'` in both branches. Fixing both while preserving their signatures:\nBoth edits applied. Now verifying with the existing test runner:\nDone. Both bugs are fixed and the existing test passes.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/config.ts`** — strict parsing: `enabled(value)` now returns `value === true` instead of `Boolean(value)`. Only the literal `true` enables the feature; falsy values and truthy-but-not-true values (`'false'`, `1`) are all disabled.\n\n2. **`src/display.ts`** — correct formatting: `display(value)` now returns `'OFF'` in the false branch instead of the duplicated `'ON'`.\n\nBoth function signatures are unchanged (API preserved), no other files were touched, and no configuration was added.\n\n**Verification** (`bun test`, the project's existing runner):\n\n```\ntest/oracle.test.ts:\n(pass) strict feature state reaches display [0.14ms]\n\n 1 pass\n 0 fail\n 6 expect() calls\n```\n\nAll 6 assertions pass — `enabled` maps `false, 'false', 1, null, undefined` → disabled → `OFF`, and only the literal `true` → `ON`."
